The basic usage is the following: (for more details we refer to the manual)

Please note: the script "secdec" is located in the main SecDec directory.
In the following, we assume that the path to the "secdec" command has been 
added to the user's default search paths, such that the secdec script can be called 
from anywhere on the user's system. Otherwise, the full path needs to be prepended to 
all secdec calls.


1) Create templates for the input files: 

secdec -prep

This command generates the  files param.input, kinem.input and math.m, 
which should be edited by the user.

2) Input the graph name and desired order in epsilon (epsord) into param.input, 
define the loop integral in math.m and specify one or more kinematic points in 
kinem.input. 

3) To run SecDec: simply issue the command 

secdec


If the input files have been renamed, they can be 
given as arguments to the secdec call as

secdec -p <myparam.input>  -m <mymath.m> -k <mykinem.input>

4) Switch to the output directory which has been created. 
It carries the graph name specified in param.input. 
Navigate to the results folder and examine the results.


A commented list of  options can be generated by
secdec -help.
